  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BCSDN Regional Civil Society Development Hub 2023-27 - Balkan Civil Society Development Hub, phase II (BCSDN)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">BCSDN Regional Civil Society Development Hub 2023-27</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">BCSDN &#xe4;r ett n&#xe4;tverk med 13 civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer (CSOs) i den vidare Balkan-regionen. BCSDN verkar f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka civilsamh&#xe4;llet och att p&#xe5;verka europeiska och nationella policys och program f&#xf6;r en b&#xe4;ttre tillvaro f&#xf6;r civilsamh&#xe4;llet som i f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngningen syftar till att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla fungerande och h&#xe5;llbara demokratier i regionen. Sida ger st&#xf6;d till BCSDN&apos;s Hub, som &#xe4;r en del av det bredare BCSDN-n&#xe4;tverket som syftar till att &#xf6;ka samarbete och motst&#xe5;ndskraft hos civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer p&#xe5; v&#xe4;stra Balkan (Albanien, Bosnien-Hercegovina, Kosovo, Montenegro, Nordmakedonien, Serbien). Programmet arbetar mot tre huvudsakliga m&#xe5;l: effektivt evidensbaserat p&#xe5;verkansarbete, &#xf6;kad f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else f&#xf6;r vikten av en m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;rande milj&#xf6; f&#xf6;r civila samh&#xe4;llet att verka samt starkare regionalt samarbete f&#xf6;r civilsamh&#xe4;llet. Programmet st&#xf6;djer bland annat arbetet med att analysera och &quot;m&#xe4;ta&quot; utrymmet f&#xf6;r det civila samh&#xe4;llet att verka i regionen. Slutsatserna fr&#xe5;n dessa studier anv&#xe4;nds i n&#xe4;tverkets p&#xe5;verkansarbete p&#xe5; nationell, regional och EU-niv&#xe5;. &#xc4;ven om BCSDN Hub framf&#xf6;r allt handlar om v&#xe4;stra Balkan-regionen med ovan n&#xe4;mna l&#xe4;nder, ing&#xe5;r Turkiet i viss m&#xe5;n genom regionalt utbyte och gemensamt p&#xe5;verkansarbete.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Balkan Civil Society Development Network is a network of 13 civil society organizations from the wider Balkan region. Its mission is to empower civil society and influence European and national policies towards a more enabling environment for civil society development to ensure sustainable and functioning democracies in the Balkans. Sida supports the BCSDN Hub, which is a program within the wider BCSDN&#x2019;s work. The Hub aims to enhance the cooperation and resilience of civil society organisations in the Western Balkans. More specifically, the Hub works within the current program towards three immediate outcomes: effective evidence-based advocacy for civic space, increased understanding of the enabling environment, and stronger regional cooperation for civic space. Among other things, the Hub supports the monitoring of the enabling environment for civil society in the Western Balkan countries and use the findings for advocacy at country, regional, and EU-levels. The BCSDN Hub focuses on the Western Balkan 6 countries to which most of the funds go, but T&#xfc;rkiye is participating in regional exchange and joint advocacy work.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ultimate outcome/impact:
Enhanced cooperation and resilience of CSOs in the Western Balkan countries that contribute to open civic space.

Intermediate outcomes
Positive changes in standards and legislation affecting the Enabling Environment for Civil Society
Increased common understanding and cooperation for promoting civic space.

Immediate outcomes:
Evidence-based advocacy for promoting the enabling environment and civic space
Improved awareness of key stakeholders about enabling environment standards and civic space state of play in the Western Balkans
Strengthened CSO and multi-stakeholder collaboration for protecting the civic space.</narrative>
  </description>
